SIMPLE  =                    T / conforms to FITS standard                      BITPIX  =                    8 / array data type                                NAXIS   =                    0 / number of array dimensions                     EXTEND  =                    T                                                  DATE    = '2026-06-30'                                                          TELESCOP= 'NuSTAR  '           / Telescope (mission) name                       INSTRUME= 'FPM     '           / Instrument name (FPM=mission-level)            ORIGIN  = 'Caltech '           / Source of FITS file                            COMMENT This FITS file may contain long string keyword values that are          COMMENT continued over multiple keywords.  This convention uses the  '&'        COMMENT character at the end of a string which is then continued                COMMENT on subsequent keywords whose name = 'CONTINUE'.                         END                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             XTENSION= 'BINTABLE'           / binary table extension                         BITPIX  =                    8 / array data type                                NAXIS   =                    2 / number of array dimensions                     NAXIS1  =                   32 / length of dimension 1                          NAXIS2  =                   92 / length of dimension 2                          PCOUNT  =                    0 / number of group parameters                     GCOUNT  =                    1 / number of groups                               TFIELDS =                    4 / number of table fields                         EXTNAME = 'NU_FINE_CLOCK'      / NuSTAR fine clock correction                   DATE    = '2026-06-30'         / Creation date                                  ORIGIN  = 'Caltech '           / Source of FITS file                            TELESCOP= 'NuSTAR  '           / Telescope (mission) name                       INSTRUME= 'FPM     '           / Instrument name (FPM=mission-level)            LONGSTRN= 'OGIP 1.0'           / The OGIP long string convention may be used.   RADECSYS= 'FK5     '           / celestial coord system                         TIMEUNIT= 's       '           / Units of header time keywords                  TASSIGN = 'SATELLITE'          / Time assigned by onboard clock                 TIMESYS = 'TT      '           / time measured from                             MJDREFI =                55197 / MJD reference day                              MJDREFF =        0.00076601852 / MJD reference (fraction of day)                TIMEREF = 'LOCAL   '           / reference time                                 VERSION =                   87 / Extension version number                       CONTENT = 'NuSTAR Fine Clock Correction' / File content                         CDES0001= 'NUSTAR FINE CLOCK CORRECTION FILE' / Description                     CCLS0001= 'BCF     '           / Dataset is a Basic Calibration File            CDTP0001= 'DATA    '           / Calibration file contains data                 CCNM0001= 'CLOCK   '           / Type of calibration data                       CVSD0001= '2010-01-01'         / UCT date when file should first be used        CVST0001= '00:00:00'           / UCT time when file should first be used        CVTD0001= '2026-06-30'         / Last UTC date when the file should be used (samCVTT0001= '2026-06-30'         / Last UTC time when the file should be used     TSTART  =          178569819.0 / [s] Start time [MET] of data in the offset fileTSTOP   =          178660815.0 / [s] Stop time [MET] of data in the offset file TTYPE1  = 'TIME    '                                                            TFORM1  = 'D       '                                                            TTYPE2  = 'CLOCK_OFF_CORR'                                                      TFORM2  = 'D       '                                                            TTYPE3  = 'CLOCK_FREQ_CORR'                                                     TFORM3  = 'D       '                                                            TTYPE4  = 'CLOCK_ERR_CORR'                                                      TFORM4  = 'D       '                                                            COMMENT This FITS file may contain long string keyword values that are          COMMENT continued over multiple keywords.  This convention uses the  '&'        COMMENT character at the end of a string which is then continued                COMMENT on subsequent keywords whose name = 'CONTINUE'.                         COMMENT                                                                         COMMENT A systematic shift of 0.0049 s was applied to the correction            COMMENT NuSTAR fine clock correction file                                       COMMENT                                                                         COMMENT         This extension contains NuSTAR 'fine' clock correction, which imCOMMENT proves                                                                  COMMENT         the NuSTAR clock performance into the 10s of microsecond range. COMMENT                                                                         COMMENT         During a transition period both kinds of extensions, the standarCOMMENT d and                                                                   COMMENT         the fine clock correction, may appear in the same FITS file.    COMMENT         Use the standard correction, or the fine correction, but not botCOMMENT h.                                                                      COMMENT         The task 'barycorr' version 2.2 and higher will automatically chCOMMENT oose                                                                    COMMENT         this extension in preference over the standard correction, if itCOMMENT  is                                                                     COMMENT         present.                                                        COMMENT                                                                         COMMENT         The extension contains the parameters of a cubic spline model.  COMMENT         The spline model represents short term clock changes driven by  COMMENT         the thermal environment of the NuSTAR observatory's clock, as   COMMENT         well as longer term stochastic drifts.                          COMMENT                                                                         COMMENT         The spline is sampled irregularly depending on changes in the   COMMENT         clock performance and thermal environment.                      COMMENT                                                                         COMMENT         Each TIME point in the table is considered a cublic spline      COMMENT         control point.  At the control point, the value of the spline   COMMENT         and its derivative are specified.  The correspond to the        COMMENT         clock *offset* (CLOCK_OFFSET, in seconds) and *frequency*       COMMENT         (CLOCK_FRACT_FREQ, expressed as a fractional quantity, or       COMMENT         seconds per second).                                            COMMENT                                                                         COMMENT         For a given epoch, t, locate the bracketing TIME samples        COMMENT         in the table.  Use cubic interpolation with the given           COMMENT         tabulated values to find the clock offset (and optionally       COMMENT         frequency) at epoch.                                            COMMENT                                                                         COMMENT         The resulting quantity is the clock correction value.  Thus,    COMMENT         this value should be *added* from observatory timestamps        COMMENT         recorded at that epoch.                                         COMMENT                                                                         HISTORY Trimmed from nuCclock20100101v230.fits.gz to the span of dummy_evt.evt bHISTORY y tools/make_test_data.py                                               END                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             A¥I„¶␀␀␀?“|'¡h>“>¸˜␀? ézpÓ0A¥IŒ†␀␀␀?“Ág;ë>Ûrxsð␀? éŸQ× A¥I”V␀␀␀?“úl:úùþ>Œ•ÖC€␀? éÆJßqóA¥Iœ&␀␀␀?”8Éâ"ZP>’1ab	p␀? éï¡2‹A¥I£ö␀␀␀?”†zÊƒü>”¸´¾␀␀? ê¡Þ©ÎA¥I«Æ␀␀␀?”Ö—^ó␀>“×“tÙ␀? êF
